# Line endings.
#
# Windows checkouts default to core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites LF to CRLF.
# That silently breaks anything a Linux container executes: `#!/bin/sh\r` is
# not a valid interpreter path, and the failure ("no such file or directory"
# for a file that plainly exists) gives no hint about line endings.
#
# Everything below must stay LF on every platform.
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.bash          text eol=lf
Dockerfile*     text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
*.sql           text eol=lf
*.conf          text eol=lf
*.properties    text eol=lf
*.py            text eol=lf
.env.example    text eol=lf
Makefile*       text eol=lf

# Binary: never touch these.
*.pdf           binary
*.parquet       binary
*.jar           binary
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
